message: "Please cite this research snapshot if you use its findings, evidence, or diagnostics."
title: "Ngramma: teacher-guided refinement of existing n-gram memory"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "crogers2287"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-07
url: "https://github.com/crogers2287/ngramma"
repository-code: "https://github.com/crogers2287/ngramma"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Research into making Flash Next's existing capabilities more reliable by
  training sparse changes to its pretrained n-gram rows with a frozen backbone.
  The first exploratory study evaluated overlay and trainer compatibility.
  The inference overlay passed narrow CPU compatibility checks, while the
  full sequence reference failed numerical agreement. No learned overlay
  or reliable task improvement was demonstrated. The release contains the
  report, numerical evidence, saved mock-tool episodes, replay verification,
  and annotated experimental source.
